{"title":"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Root\">zeros</a>, the product of the zeros, and the sum of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coefficient\" title=\"Coefficient\">coefficients</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf34a339362e0ff0d2d7ffd1f49e4af029a7ca4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=ax^{2}+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" /> are equal. Their common value must also be which of the following? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/964b00c9f7e6439b7bc27f1f9dd708b28c0f91bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{(A)}\\ \\textrm{the\\ coefficient\\ of\\ }x^{2}~~~ \\textrm{(B)}\\ \\textrm{the\\ coefficient\\ of\\ }x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"355\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2af53481be050d1b950fed002213742b0f009313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{(C)}\\ \\textrm{the\\ y-intercept\\ of\\ the\\ graph\\ of\\ }y=f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"324\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce1ecfe49c439b5938bf9d752be7a18c2f815be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{(D)}\\ \\textrm{one\\ of\\ the\\ x-intercepts\\ of\\ the\\ graph\\ of\\ }y=f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"381\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbe750773d618584a11917f253e97d77c50e6a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{(E)}\\ \\textrm{the\\ mean\\ of\\ the\\ x-intercepts\\ of\\ the\\ graph\\ of\\ }y=f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"422\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a>, the sum of the roots of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">quadratic equation</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69adcf50f5152711464f6d19c156782cb894ae3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {-b}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"37\" />,  the product of the zeros is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd38c0b006565bd66f7cdf9f9a3cbfa955673f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />, and the sum of the coefficients is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />. Setting equal the first two tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab386776004a2e966c99eb2b1b2e69f31239af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {-b}{a} = \\frac ca \\Rightarrow b = -c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c03697e404927ba1f9df0d81727302bd6c356413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = a + b - b = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"197\" height=\"14\" />, so the common value is also equal to the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5aaea5f5a0c59fbe5728346845f4340e2dfe32e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 \\Longrightarrow \\fbox{\\textrm{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p>To disprove the others, note that:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0630a19ec36e5e78a5a38b29446b59f240a3f75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{B}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />: then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d49f94f216301e2069778d62824d2acb8282c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac {-b}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"56\" height=\"37\" />, which is not necessarily true.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/5875c5dc39c062d1166ed1e25f1258033fc0d9b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{C}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />: the y-intercept is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e81179b6de9066673e2aab733f36d0ff90a581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"33\" />, not necessarily true.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d45378143e9d318692101f621a56b88327d722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{D}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />: an x-intercept of the graph is a root of the polynomial, but this excludes the other root.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07e655cd29678d48f0577dc2f5c5d1dda102c12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />: the mean of the x-intercepts will be the sum of the roots of the quadratic divided by 2.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A\">2007 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Probl